Z||000000||Olsson||07-25-2001||05:45 AM||||Hello!<BR>im thinking of buying a Fiero GT with the V6-engine. Its a beautiful car but I dont now so much about it.. does it have any weakness? or is it just a great car?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>how are the car to drive? how fast is it? are there some simple mods to do that makes it go faster?<BR>sorry if my english isnt the best...<BR>/Olsson from Sweden||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||07-25-2001||06:14 AM||||A fun car to drive.  Remember it is a 15 year old car, parts may be hard to find, especially in Sweden.<P>Top speed 120 mph+ in stock form.  No such thing as simple mods that will make it go faster.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||hyhy4u||07-25-2001||10:15 AM||||The cars a blast to drive! But the car does need a ton of attention or it will just kindof fall apart in front of you.  And parts, escpecially for the GT are pertty tough sometimes to come by..but all in all i would defidently say its worth it!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Steve Normington||07-25-2001||10:40 AM||||Is it an 88 or a pre-88? The 88's are <u>very</u> hard to find parts for. If it is a manual transmission, test the clutch to make sure it engages/disengages smoothly. Check the headlight motors to make sure they work. When the engine is running, listen for any clatter in the engine. If you can jack up the car, test the wheels to make sure there is no lateral movement. With the engine in first, spin one of the tires back and forth and listen for any clunking. With a small mirror, look at the forward exhaust manifold for cracks/looseness.<P>If you do buy this car, you'll want to replace the belts and hoses. You might want to replace all the vacuum hoses too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||07-25-2001||10:41 AM||||maybe cliff will respond to this or try to contact him. i hear he's in the states now but from your neck of the woods sorta. he could probaly give you the most knowledgeable comparisions bettween fieros and other cars available to you and maintenance/parts/service related to it from a perspective of where you live.||||reg||1
